  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A working event record",
    "overview": "A quiet CRM shell puts the event, its current drafts, and the next action ahead of decoration. Pale navigation, compact controls, thin dividers, and white reading surfaces carry the workspace. The coordinator can open source evidence without losing the current draft.\n\nThe owner supplied the [AI CRM dashboard reference](https://21st.dev/@larsen66/templates/ai-crm-dashboard) and [opportunities preview](https://21st-crm.vercel.app/opportunities). This is a code-led visual adaptation, not copied template source. No paid template was purchased or downloaded. Existing Yanni's sidebar SVG geometry, event-list count behavior, and EventBrief's evidence interaction remain part of the implemented system. [Attribution](docs/ATTRIBUTION.md) records the reuse boundary.\n\nThis system describes the `/package` workspace. The older three-field extraction page and the copied printable document templates have their own retained styles; their values do not become dashboard defaults.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale navigation and white reading surfaces",
      "Thin dividers with gently rounded controls",
      "Written readiness and review states",
      "Source-linked facts",
      "Simple next actions"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Written State Rule",
        "body": "Always pair state color with its visible state text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Workspace Rule",
        "body": "Use existing fills, borders, and focus treatment to distinguish states instead of introducing shadow-based cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Actual Progress Rule",
        "body": "Display real saved results and review counts; do not invent agent activity or confidence metrics.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep authored examples distinct from AI results.",
      "**Do** use written state labels alongside color.",
      "**Do** keep source evidence reachable from the selected draft.",
      "**Do** preserve visible focus and the mobile stacked layout."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** label an unreviewed draft approved.",
      "**Don't** add decorative charts or invented agent progress.",
      "**Don't** apply the old extraction page's purple tokens to new event-workspace surfaces.",
      "**Don't** treat printed document styling as the dashboard's component system."
    ]
  }
}
